{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9yHSfBWjKFJC2hCycjT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`fd` now checks every `--and` pattern for path separators, not just the main pattern. Before, `fd foo --and one/two` silently printed nothing; now it gives the same \"contains a path-separation character\" error, naming the pattern that caused it.\n\n- **`src/main.rs`:** the separator check moved into a small helper, `pattern_contains_path_separator`. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` runs it on the main pattern and then each `--and` pattern, and errors on the first one that contains a separator. The rules haven't changed: `/` always triggers the error, and on Windows `\\` triggers it only if the pattern names an existing directory. `--full-path` still skips the check.\n- **`tests/tests.rs`:** added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`.\n\nTest results:\n- The new test failed before the fix with no error output, and passes after it. With the `src/main.rs` change reverted, it fails again.\n- The full suite passes (139 + 111 tests, 0 failed).\n- `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` is clean for the source code.\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets` reports errors in `tests/tests.rs` (such as the redundant `&` at line 2539). They're in code I didn't touch and appear without my change too, so I left them alone.\n- The Windows `\\` branch wasn't compiled or run, since this machine is Linux.\n\nOn `--and`, the error's suggestion `fd . '<pattern>'` doesn't quite fit, but I kept one message for both cases. Nothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":42593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":420,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":nul